":0,"issues":0,"language":"JavaScript","description":"copy and paste script into browser console window to find github repo links and print them out sequentially","topics":[],"score":2115,"global_rank":271747},{"name":"darkblue94/recipe-app","owner":"darkblue94","html_url":"https://github.com/darkblue94/recipe-app","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"JavaScript","description":"I created a web-app with React that makes API calls to \"food2fork.com\" , reviving an object that contains Recipes Names , Links, Publishers and Images. I target my input element of 'name' and pass its value into a const variable which I  concatenate in the url that is being fetched. I take all that data into my state, pass it as a prop in my Recipes component and I use the map function to unbox every instance of a recipe that contains the main ingredient searched by the user. ","topics":[],"score":2115,"global_rank":271748},{"name":"darkblue94/react-step-form","owner":"darkblue94","html_url":"https://github.com/darkblue94/react-step-form","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"JavaScript","description":"Here I create a fluid , step form with React. A step form is a form broken down into steps. Here I create a step for \"FirstName,LastName,Email\", a second step for \"Instrument,City,Bio\", a third step for a chance for the user to review and confirm the date the put into the form. I use State and props to keep track of the step I was in(0-4). With functions like nextStep and prevStep I was able to add or take away form state.step. The value of Step determines what I Component I have UserForm return.","topics":[],"score":2115,"global_rank":271749},{"name":"darkblue94/weather-app","owner":"darkblue94","html_url":"https://github.com/darkblue94/weather-app","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"JavaScript","description":"Find Out The Weather Conditions In Your City Of Choice. I used React.js to build the components and https://openweathermap